    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1072" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχοῦ</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγχι</span>
			, <i>near</i>, freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, usu. in phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχοῦ δ᾽
			ἱσταμένη</span> (or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ος</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.172
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεῦται δ᾽ Ὀδυσῆος ἀκοῦσαι ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.526
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				19.271
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καθῆσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archil.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					3.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				962
			</span></i>: twice c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.709
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.5
			</span></i>: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				9.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.85
			</span></i>: in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι ἀ. τούτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
				</span></i>
			<i>V A</i><i><span class="en">
				6.16
			</span></i>.</div>
